690 0 obj
<<
/Title (extended beyond standard workflow actions by combining a reusable Deluge custom function with a serverless Zoho Catalyst function. The worked example assigns a service-priority level to a submitted vehicle request using details such as vehicle age, service type, breakdown status and urgency. Creator sends the request data to the external function and uses the returned priority to update the service record. The code and workflow in this report are illustrative and are not presented as a deployed implementation.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 645 0 R
/Prev 689 0 R
>>
endobj
691 0 obj
<<
/Title (When a service request is submitted, a Creator workflow calls the Deluge function. The function sends the selected request fields through a managed HTTPS connection to Catalyst. Catalyst validates the values, applies the example rules and returns a JSON priority. Creator can then update the request record.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 527 0 R
/Prev 646 0 R
/Next 647 0 R
>>
endobj
